s how do I explain the  900 files at the at the White House I  cannot I that particular part of the  FBI's responsibility never came under my  authority that was in the what was used  to be called records management but we  had a very very rigorous standard about  sending summary reports to the White  House they had to be requested by the  White House Counsel it had to be on an  individual we knew was under  investigation for clearance for a White  House job or a high-level appointment  and they were very closely tracked and  carefully monitored it of course is  absolutely unacceptable for FBI files or  reports to be used for any sort of  partisan political purposes or to gain  advantage over one's political  adversaries and that's one thing of  significant interest I'll be watching in  ken starr's reports as to what the  bottom line is on on that particular  situation yes sir  do you think the probabilities will seem  attacked by the 21st century and the  question is weapons of mass destruction  what is the probability of attack and  what kind of target well I have to say  that I believe that the conventional  weapons of terrorists will continue to  be the most prevalent bombs have been  very effective for terrorists and they  are very easy to make and very easy to  deploy but if you really want to make a  statement if you want to traumatize the  society look at what the Amish in Riccio  did with sarin gas in Tokyo that cats  out of the bag there are now available  on the international market gas and  biological materials as well as some  radiological materials that can be  utilized and in fact someday will be  utilized and probably not in a too  distant future and they'll pick a target  that is not defended they'll pick an  easy target because they are not  concerned with mid  three advantage they're concerned with  traumatizing a society punishing a  society so they will choose something  like the World Trade Center you know no  value from a standpoint of strateg