s that with  the FBI and CIA on a specific as-needed  basis and with the CIA on a continuing  basis but it is a military organization  for signals intelligence the DIA is an  umbrella organization for the collection  of intelligence for specific military  purposes both its analysis and its  collection are geared towards the  military needs of the United States  whereas the CIA is an umbrella  organization for all other intelligence  activities including bringing in the  military intelligence components the  CIA's relationship with the FBI in spite  of what we read is a very positive one I  think certainly the bombings in East  Africa obviously the intelligence that  came from that was not FBI intelligence  that was CIA based and dia based  intelligence and it was integrated quite  quickly into the FBI's investigation the  FBI on the other hand is a an agency of  the Justice Department and is the  principal investigative and  counterintelligence agency of the United  States government it does not work for  the CIA or under the umbrella of the CIA  but it works together with the CIA and  as part of the intelligence community  the CIA director wears two hats he's the  director of the CIA and the director of  the US intelligence community there he  has a coordination and budget  authorization role and the FBI of  it's counterintelligence and  counterterrorism budgets pass through  that process so there is a very closely  related coordination between these  organizations but their functions and  their activities are very different yes  sir  facing the FBI going into the next  century both internally and experts I  think one of the largest challenges in  this sounds parochial I don't mean it to  be because we now have a hundred and  forty four separate federal agencies  going out in different directions  without any coordination without any any  direction or control and no one's in  charge no one's in charge as we go into  the 21st century  and we're faced with the global